<item><title>Niger bans peanut exports, with exceptions possible for Mali</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ml/niger-bans-peanut-exports-with-exceptions-possible-for-mali-311a38/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ml/niger-bans-peanut-exports-with-exceptions-possible-for-mali-311a38/</guid><category>Mali</category><description>The ban, set by an order dated 11 November, is meant to supply Niger&apos;s cooking-oil processing plants with local raw material.</description><pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 02:39:29 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ml.jpg" length="29829" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ml.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Mali names police commissioner Moussa Ag Infahi inspector general of security services</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ml/mali-names-police-commissioner-moussa-ag-infahi-inspector-3fae9b/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ml/mali-names-police-commissioner-moussa-ag-infahi-inspector-3fae9b/</guid><category>Mali</category><description>The appointment places a veteran national police officer in charge of security and civil protection services, a post Mali&apos;s Council of Ministers filled on Friday.</description><pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 02:00:42 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ml.jpg" length="29829" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ml.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Mali beats Rwanda 3-2 to take sole lead of CAN 2027 qualifying Group K</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ml/mali-beats-rwanda-3-2-to-take-sole-lead-of-can-2027-675098/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ml/mali-beats-rwanda-3-2-to-take-sole-lead-of-can-2027-675098/</guid><category>Mali</category><description>Mali came from behind twice at the 26-Mars Stadium in Bamako, with Kamory Doumbia equalising after a Rwandan goalkeeping error and Camara&apos;s 84th-minute strike sealing the result.</description><pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 21:24:15 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ml.jpg" length="29829" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ml.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Inheritance disputes leave widows and orphans in Mali without their share</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ml/inheritance-disputes-leave-widows-and-orphans-in-mali-ade1c2/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ml/inheritance-disputes-leave-widows-and-orphans-in-mali-ade1c2/</guid><category>Mali</category><description>Relatives of deceased heads of family are reportedly sharing out property in disregard of the rights of widows and children.</description><pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 17:30:00 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/ml/inheritance-disputes-leave-widows-and-orphans-in-mali-ade1c2/share.jpg" length="40679" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/ml/inheritance-disputes-leave-widows-and-orphans-in-mali-ade1c2/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
